# SQLite backup schedule example
#
# Install on the host running docker compose. Replace APP_DIR with the
# absolute repository path before installing this entry in root's or the
# deployment user's crontab.
#
# The backup utility uses SQLite's online-backup API and writes into the
# mounted ./data volume. It refuses to overwrite an existing backup.
#
# Daily at 03:15 UTC:
15 3 * * * cd /opt/autonomous-business-manager && docker compose exec -T app python deploy/backup_database.py >> /var/log/autonomous-business-manager-backup.log 2>&1

# Operational requirements:
# - Keep /opt/autonomous-business-manager/data/backups on protected storage.
# - Monitor the cron log for failures.
# - Copy backups to separate durable storage; a backup on the same disk is not disaster recovery.
# - Periodically run deploy/restore_database.py against a test destination and verify application startup.
# - Never place .env, encryption keys, or other credentials in the backup destination's public path.
